.TH MULTI-SETTINGS 1 "September 2026" "Multi Settings 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
multi-settings \- manage Ubuntu accounts, YubiKeys, and system hardening
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B multi-settings
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B multi-settings
starts the native GTK 4 Multi Settings application.
It can create local users, enroll YubiKeys, configure password plus YubiKey
authentication, and audit or apply DevSec OS and SSH hardening.
.PP
The graphical application runs as the current user. Operations that modify
the system are delegated to a PolicyKit-authorized helper.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/multi-settings/custom-settings.yml
User-selected Ansible settings that override the hardening role defaults.
.TP
.I /var/lib/multi-settings
Protected application state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/wRRM/multi-settings/issues.
